  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional Strengthening Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Main activities and objectives under the Institutional Strengthening Project are as following: - Phase IV: Monitoring the ODS import and consumption data; following up with priority the issue of initiating measures to improve HCFC control according to the phase-out schedule of the Protocol; monitoring the HPMP implementation; tracking the promulgation and enforcement of policy and legislation with a specific focus on HCFC management; implementing needed measures in refrigeration air-conditioning sector; capacity building of the ozone unit; and data reporting to the Fund and Ozone Secretariats. - Phase V: Monitor the ODS import and consumption data which is defined by regulation at State level and entities level; further improve and harmonize the regulation; monitor the HPMP implementation; focus on HCFC management and assist in the development of the appropriate activities for the HPMP implementation; and control of HCFCs containing equipment through regulatory process; and data reporting to the Fund and Ozone Secretariats. - Phase VI: Continue monitoring the licensing system and allocate quotas against the records of customs to control HCFC imports; implement regulatory control focusing on reducing HCFC-based equipment on the market; cooperate with custom authorities including training; monitor the HPMP implem</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Montreal Protocol</narrative>
  </participating-org>
